      "message": "I\u0027ll wait to hear from you on the other CL regarding the first part.\n\nRe: ancestor: It should be ok for these to come after the S4 state introduction. With only the S4 state patch and not this one, the SLP_S4 and SLP_S5 lines start out merged via this bit in intel_x86.h:\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_HOSTCMD_ESPI_VW_SLP_S5\n...\n#else\n#define SLP_S5_SIGNAL_L SLP_S4_SIGNAL_L\n#endif\n\nSo the state machines observes SLP_S4 and SLP_S5 change at the same time, effectively causing us to always slide right through the S4 state. I tested this on my volteer system and it seemed to work.",
